  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p><em>Our anger is a glorious wave which rolls and churns like the ocean’s tide.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Prerequisites:</strong> Ki pool class feature, rage class feature.</p>\n<p><strong>Benefit:</strong> Whenever you spend one or more ki points while raging, you may extend the duration of any rage-like effect you are under by 1 round (such as the rage spell or the Disciple of Chaos’s practiced anger ability) or maintain your barbarian rage without expending a round of rage at the start of your next turn.</p>\n<p>Your ki pool increases by 1. If your rage ability is measured in rounds per day, you can rage for 3 additional rounds per day.</p>\n<p><strong>Note:</strong> The barbarian’s rage normally prevents abilities that require “patience or concentration”. Ki powers do not technically require either although some GMs might limit a barbarian from using their ki powers during a rage; if so, the Roiling Anger feat allows you to use ki powers while raging if you could not already.</p>\n<p><sup><strong>Source:</strong> Diamond Classes: Disciple of Chaos</sup></p>\n<p><a href=\"http://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/general-feats#toc61\">Source: Spheres of Power Wiki</a></p>",
      "instructions": ""
    },
